    "text": "Excellent! I've successfully implemented a bounded stack in Cuis Smalltalk with comprehensive test coverage.\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n**BoundedStack Class** (category: BoundedStack)\n- `initialize: aCapacity` - Creates the stack and validates capacity (must be positive integer)\n- `push: anObject` - Adds objects; fails with \"stack is full\" when at capacity\n- `pop` - Removes and returns the top element; fails with \"stack is empty\" when empty\n- `top` - Returns the top element without removing; fails with \"stack is empty\" when empty\n- `isEmpty` - Returns whether the stack is empty\n- `size` - Returns current stack size\n- `new: aCapacity` - Class method for creating bounded stacks\n\n**Test Suite** (category: BoundedStack-Tests)\n21 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Stack creation with valid/invalid capacities\n- Push operations and full stack handling\n- Pop and top operations with proper LIFO behavior\n- State methods (isEmpty, size)\n- All error conditions with correct error messages\n- Edge cases (capacity 1 and 100)\n- Different object types\n\n**Test Results**: \u2705 **21/21 tests passing**\n\nThe implementation is complete and fully tested. All behaviors described in the requirements are implemented and verified."
